# Gadget YAML Reference
Key fields and structure of gadget.yaml for Ubuntu Core gadget snaps.

## Minimal structure
```yaml
volumes:
  pc:
    bootloader: grub
    structure:
      - name: ubuntu-seed
        role: system-seed
        type: EF,C12A7328-F81F-11D2-BA4B-00A0C93EC93B
        filesystem: vfat
        size: 1200M
      - name: ubuntu-boot
        role: system-boot
        filesystem: ext4
        size: 750M
      - name: ubuntu-save
        role: system-save
        filesystem: ext4
        size: 16M
      - name: ubuntu-data
        role: system-data
        filesystem: ext4
        size: 1G
```

## Top-level keys

**volumes**        Map of disk volumes. Most devices have one (e.g. "pc", "pi").
**defaults**       Default snap configuration applied at first boot.
                   Format: defaults: <snap-id>: key: value
**connections**    Interface connections made automatically at first boot.
**device-tree**    Path to device tree blob (ARM/embedded boards).
**device-tree-origin** Where to find the dtb: gadget or kernel.

## Structure roles (required)

system-seed        Contains model assertion and seeded snaps (FAT32).
system-boot        Boot assets: kernel.efi, grub, recovery kernels.
system-save        Persists across factory reset: device keys, save data.
system-data        Main user data partition. Contains snapd state.

## Structure fields

name               Human-readable partition name (used by idiot, sfdisk).
role               One of: system-seed, system-boot, system-save, system-data.
type               Partition type GUID or short code (e.g. 83 for Linux data).
filesystem         vfat, ext4, or none (for raw partitions).
filesystem-label   Label shown to tools like blkid.
size               Partition size: e.g. 1200M, 2G. Last partition may use
                   "min-size" to grow to fill the disk.
content            List of files/dirs to copy into the partition at build time.
update             Controls what happens to this partition during gadget update.

## defaults example
```yaml
defaults:
  <snapd-snap-id>:
    refresh.schedule: "00:00-24:00/2"
  <my-app-snap-id>:
    server.port: 8080
```

## connections example
```yaml
connections:
  - plug: <my-app-snap-id>:network-observe
```

## Full disk encryption
To enable FDE, the model assertion must include:
  storage-safety: encrypted

The gadget must support the UC FDE hook. ubuntu-save must be present.

